  <p>
    I'm Christopher — a country and economic risk analyst covering mainland Southeast Asia
    (Vietnam, Cambodia, Laos, Thailand, Myanmar), with broader ASEAN experience across Indonesia.
    My research combines country-level political economy with quantitative methods — recent work
    spans Vietnam's exposure to US tariff policy, the political economy of Indonesia's capital
    relocation, and how the Vietnamese party-state's governance structures shaped its COVID-19
    response (<a href="/research">see Research</a>). I'm now writing that same analysis for news
    outlets and online magazines, and I run
    <a href="https://mekong-advisory-main.vercel.app">Mekong Advisory</a>, an independent
    consultancy producing it for institutional clients.
  </p>

  <p>
    I spent four years living and building a consultancy in Hà Nội, developing on-the-ground
    knowledge of Vietnam's regulatory environment, business landscape, and policy dynamics. I
    speak, read, and write Vietnamese at an advanced level, with working Bahasa Indonesia and
    elementary Thai. My graduate training combines an MA in Southeast Asian Studies
    (<a href="https://www.soas.ac.uk/">SOAS, University of London</a>, Distinction) with an MSc in
    Development Economics (<a href="http://www.city.ac.uk">City, University of London</a>,
    Distinction), giving me both the area-studies depth and the quantitative toolkit to produce
    policy- and investment-relevant analysis of the region.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>I'm actively pitching analysis and explainer pieces to news outlets and magazines.</strong>
    If you're an editor looking for mainland Southeast Asia coverage — political risk, trade
    exposure, state capacity, development economics — get in touch.
  </p>

