  <h2>Regional Focus</h2>

  <p>
    Vietnam is my primary country focus. I have direct experience navigating its regulatory
    environment, working with Vietnamese businesses and counterparts, and tracking its economic
    and policy trajectory — from the trade-driven growth of the 2010s through the post-pandemic
    pivot and the current US tariff pressure on its export sector. I bring the same
    governance-first framework to Cambodia's debt dynamics, Laos's power-export model, Myanmar's
    post-coup economy, and Thailand's political cycles. My broader ASEAN coverage spans Indonesia
    and the region's comparative development dynamics, with analytical focus on investment
    environments, state capacity, and economic governance.
  </p>

  <h2>Background</h2>

  <p>
    From 2016 to 2020, I co-founded and ran a technology consultancy based in Hà Nội, working
    with clients across Vietnam, Indonesia, and Thailand. That experience gave me practical
    knowledge of how businesses operate, fail, and succeed in Southeast Asian regulatory
    environments — knowledge I now apply analytically. Before Vietnam, I spent nearly a decade
    in software development and data analysis roles in the US, including at
    <a href="https://www.novachem.com">NOVA Chemicals</a>. Since returning to graduate school,
    I have worked as an economic research analyst at
    <a href="https://www.alleghenyecon.com">Allegheny Economic Research</a>, producing
    policy-relevant quantitative research and client-facing reports for government and
    private-sector stakeholders.
  </p>

  <p>
    Founder, <a href="https://mekong-advisory-main.vercel.app">Mekong Advisory</a> — an independent
    economic consultancy focused on the Greater Mekong Subregion (Vietnam, Thailand, Cambodia,
    Laos, Myanmar), producing evidence-based analysis for policymakers, institutions, and
    investors.
  </p>

  <h2>For Editors</h2>

  <p>
    I pitch analysis and explainer pieces on mainland Southeast Asia — political risk, trade and
    investment exposure, state capacity, and development economics. Recent work includes an
    analysis of Vietnam's exposure to US tariff policy, an MA dissertation on how Vietnam's
    party-state governance shaped its COVID-19 response, and a policy brief on Indonesia's capital
    relocation (<a href="/research">see Research</a> for details). I also run
    <a href="https://mekong-advisory-main.vercel.app">Mekong Advisory</a>, an independent
    consultancy covering the same region for institutional clients. Reach me at
    <a href="mailto:chrisjoy@sent.com">chrisjoy@sent.com</a>.
  </p>

